{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture","id":1051415,"title":"I can't wrap my head around W:tA... help me get a clear picture?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-19T01:16:33-08:00","id":1051415,"title":"I can't wrap my head around W:tA... help me get a clear picture?","content":"As it relates to the overall &quot;World of Darkness&quot; anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u2022So you are this ultimate manifestation of mother nature's primal fury made flesh... in order to combat spiritual evils that, more often than not, don't require fang and claw to defeat.<br /> \u200b\u2022The overall villain of the setting is the slow (or not so slow?) and subtle (or not so subtle?) corruption of the natural world, but you can't really do anything about it because the tribes just can't quit in-fighting.<br /> \u200b\u2022There doesn't seem to be any &quot;personal horror&quot; in this game, as you have complete control of your character except for a frenzy, and unlike in VtM, frenzying isn't necessarily a bad thing?<br /> <br /> \u200bI know my breakdown is probably wrong (I've never had a chance to actually play in a game), but from other people's stories and such, that's the impression I got.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat is a better description of W:tA that may better capture what the game and it's setting are about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12985-schwann145","name":"Schwann145","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:25:30-08:00","id":1051417,"title":"","content":"A group of racist stereotypes band together to serve as homicidal primitivist ecoterrorists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T03:24:32-08:00","id":1051447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwann145</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture#post1051415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u2022So you are this ultimate manifestation of mother nature's primal fury made flesh... in order to combat spiritual evils that, more often than not, don't require fang and claw to defeat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sorta. Keep in mind that werewolves were created deep in pre-history, when more of these evils were capable of being defeated with fang and claw. And while not necessarily the core of the setting, the werewolves were not created to solve these problems alone, they're the ones the were made to be fighty and they're the majority of what's left in modern times whether or not fighty solutions are the best ones.<br /> <br /> There's also plenty in the game dealing with the current difficulty of defeating the enemy being because the enemy figured out that it can send lots of fighty threats to keep the Garou distracted while it figured out how to corrupt its way into all sorts of things that can't be easily solved with fighty solutions. A recurring theme in the game is that most of the setbacks the Garou are dealing with today are largely of their own making (or at least their ancestors making).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022The overall villain of the setting is the slow (or not so slow?) and subtle (or not so subtle?) corruption of the natural world, but you can't really do anything about it because the tribes just can't quit in-fighting. </div> </div> </div>This is the pessimistic view of things. Largely things got as bad as they did because the Garou suck at getting along, but with the signs of the Apocalypse at hand, the voices for a unified front are starting to win out over the ones that want to keep fighting the same multi-generational feuds. The question is whether the Garou can unify fast enough, and sufficiently to cope with what's about to happen or not. And even if they can, how much of whatever they can do that will count as a lasting victory is still questionable.<br /> <br /> It's far less, &quot;all is lost because we're constantly at each others' throats,&quot; and more, &quot;all will be lost if we don't stop going at each others' throats, and even after we fix that we don't know if we'll do it in time.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022There doesn't seem to be any &quot;personal horror&quot; in this game, as you have complete control of your character except for a frenzy, and unlike in VtM, frenzying isn't necessarily a bad thing? </div> </div> </div>Eh? I mean, mechanically there's not that much &quot;personal horror&quot; in any of the WoD games. There is however plenty of potential for it even if most WtA games tend to go for the action horror angle instead. Keep in mind that all werewolves give off an aura of &quot;I'm a dangerous nasty angry big bad wolf&quot; that makes interacting with normal people difficult for all but the lowest Rage characters, becoming a werewolf is horrifically traumatic (that majority of Homids are stated to have killed someone during their First Change, Metis are deformed outcasts, and Lupus suddenly have a human level mind shoved into their formerly wolf-like brains out of the blue without any build up to prepare them for the on rush of experience that represents) and the only people that know what's happening to you are also trying to induct you into a warrior cult. There's a lot of room for personal horror if you want to explore it.<br /> <br /> Frenzying in WtA is never a good thing, it's just sometimes better than the other options. As well, if you're at temporary or permanent Rage of 4+, Frenzies start getting extremely dangerous unless you have a shit ton of Willpower. And Frenzies can be triggered by <b>good</b> things if they're too strong (notably any extremely strong emotion can overwhelm a werewolf, so getting to wrapped up in love can cause you to flip out and kill your lover... which is pretty personal horror).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bWhat is a better description of W:tA that may better capture what the game and it's setting are about? </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that it's a big game that's about a lot of things. Everything you said is a perfectly valid way to play the game. It's less wrong and more narrow view of the possibilities of what you can do with it.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Lex's response. She's not wrong, it's just not the only thing you can do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:33:40-08:00","id":1051514,"title":"","content":"The Fera are the only defenders of the biosphere and seemingly the only supernatural entities to understand enough ecology to realize that humanity is on the path to annihilate itself along with the rest of the life on Earth (including the Fera). For the Fera, it is a fight of self-preservation because they cannot exist without wild members of their animal species in existence. While the Ananasi, Corax, and Ratkin might be able to survive until humanity completely destroys the biosphere, even they would go extinct at the end of all life.<br /> <br /> Garou are among the fiercest defenders of humanity because they are trying to prevent humanity from committing murder-suicide with the rest of the biosphere (and, to a greater or lesser extent, so are the rest of the Fera, though their methods are different than the methods of the Garou). The Garou seek to destroy Pentex, which is trying to convert the entirety of humanity into Fomori, and to change the behaviors of the rest of corporations and governments through a mixture of education, political action, and whistleblowing (with some old fashion sabotage and violence thrown in). They do not only seek to preserve the wilderness from the Wyrm though, they also seek to beautify and preserve urban area from the Wyrm. Whether it is killing the parasites that make urban life awful (loan sharks, slum lords, white slavers, etc) or just making sure the the urban poor have access to parks, they are the only group of supernatural creatures that actually care about the fate of the downtrodden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T11:48:05-08:00","id":1051596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051417#post1051417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A group of racist stereotypes band together to serve as homicidal primitivist ecoterrorists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has been steadily getting rid of those (and most of them are actually ethnic/country stereotypes, since some of the most stilted ones came from European tribes) since about the time the older Silver Fangs tribebook came out and revealed that they actually have a native presence everywhere but the Americas and Antarctica. Revised and W20 did a lot more work along these lines, such as the Get of Fenris being revealed to be much more diverse and killing off the Swords of Heimdall for being racist tools, or the Silent Striders tribebook clearing up any misconceptions about the Rroma being related to them (not any more than any other group of humans), and how Pure Breed only has anything to do with werewolf tribe heritage and not human ethnicity (it needs to be renamed like how Past Lives became Ancestors, but with the modern WW... ugh, that might not just not happen, we could backslide for the first edition instead of making leaps ahead). Croatan Song, for all that it gets panned for being boring and dry, also established that the so-called Pure Lands weren't, and that the three werewolf tribes of the Americas were actually pretty occupied fighting monsters and slick-tongued corrupters looking to set up shops in the major cities on the continent.<br /> <br /> As for the second part? Context is everything. A notable minority of werewolves are actually wolfweres, were never brought up as humans, and don't share human sensibilities, even considering that being part-spirit means that they still aren't actually human. They also have a close kinship with beings that aren't even material or made of flesh and often want to see their domains revitalized. Which is difficult when two tribes see less inherently wrong with modern life, and have agreements with spirits of technology and modern materials that they, likewise, don't want to endanger. Because spirit is everything; unlike in Exalted, in Werewolf, the god <i>is</i> the river. Also, they have a history of having hunted humans in ancient times, and the Mokole actually shaped humans from early primates, since they were left over from an earlier struggle with similar character... and arguably fucked up even worse than the Garou have, per Shattered Dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:01:56-08:00","id":1051625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwann145</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture#post1051415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it relates to the overall &amp;quot;World of Darkness&amp;quot; anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u2022So you are this ultimate manifestation of mother nature's primal fury made flesh... in order to combat spiritual evils that, more often than not, don't require fang and claw to defeat.<br /> \u200b\u2022The overall villain of the setting is the slow (or not so slow?) and subtle (or not so subtle?) corruption of the natural world, but you can't really do anything about it because the tribes just can't quit in-fighting.<br /> \u200b\u2022There doesn't seem to be any &amp;quot;personal horror&amp;quot; in this game, as you have complete control of your character except for a frenzy, and unlike in VtM, frenzying isn't necessarily a bad thing?<br /> <br /> \u200bI know my breakdown is probably wrong (I've never had a chance to actually play in a game), but from other people's stories and such, that's the impression I got.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat is a better description of W:tA that may better capture what the game and it's setting are about?</div> </div> </div> </div>A better description is: a bunch of hellhounds on steroids, living as new age hippies in the woods, playing Captain Planet.<br /> <br /> WtA has always been a silly game to be. From all the WoD games, it has always been the one I liked the least, and the one I considered the less profound of meaning, of mysticism, of substance.<br /> <br /> That being said, the concept of the Uratha, the Werewolves from the Forsaken game of the new world of darkness (chronicles of darkness) really got my attention. For one, it removed that captain ecology thing which always stricked me as being so silly, and second, it introduced a sense of horror that actually grasped my attention. I'll look into it further","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:19:12-08:00","id":1051632,"title":"","content":"Ofc WtA players will try to crucify me for saying this, but it is my opnion nevertheless, I don't care if the players of werewolf think their fanatical love of the game, I won't change my mind just because people get mad for being spoken about. It's a silly and pointless game, no one needs to agree with me, but you can all deal with the fact that that's how many people see this game.<br /> <br /> Ideal if you like shallow 2 dimensions heroes/villains, and if you love games based on random mayhem and violence and little actual roleplay, social interactions or intelectual pursuit.<br /> <br /> Fomori and other Wyrm-crap are utter villains, Garou and Fera are the heroes. Very black and white. Have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:49:41-08:00","id":1051651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051632#post1051632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ofc WtA players will try to crucify me for saying this, but it is my opnion nevertheless, I don't care if the players of werewolf think their fanatical love of the game, I won't change my mind just because people get mad for being spoken about. It's a silly and pointless game, no one needs to agree with me, but you can all deal with the fact that that's how many people see this game.<br /> <br /> Ideal if you like shallow 2 dimensions heroes/villains, and if you love games based on random mayhem and violence and little actual roleplay, social interactions or intelectual pursuit.<br /> <br /> Fomori and other Wyrm-crap are utter villains, Garou and Fera are the heroes. Very black and white. Have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are entitled to your own opinion, but is there any reason why you'd come into the forum of a game you dislike and shit all over it? There are some White Wolf games I dislike, so I just don't visit those forums.<br /> <br /> But, back on topic.<br /> <br /> While on the surface, Werewolf is a violent, black and white game, they are a few aspects of the game I find fascinating:<br /> <br /> 1. Kinfolk. Family has always been a central component to any character I create. Werewolf has family built into the system. Unable to interact well with Humanity, the Garou desperately need their Kinfolk. Vampires can just Ghoul another daytime assistant, but a Garou can't replace their younger brother. Kinfolk provide a much needed connection to Humanity/Lupine side that can not be easily replaced.<br /> <br /> 2. Religion. I like to Role Play to explore religious concepts, but find that people get offended if I use real life religions to do this. Gaia allows me to explore the religious topics such as faith, fanaticism, and doubt, without stepping on the toes of other player's religious beliefs.<br /> <br /> 3. Politics. I like Werewolf politics better than Vampire politics because Garou argue about how to go about saving the Gaia from the Wyrm rather than backstab their fellow sept members due to self interest.<br /> <br /> 4. Alien Viewpoints. In D&amp;D, I rarely play a human character despite the mechanical advantages. I always play a different race. In Werewolf, I can play a Wolf trying to adapt to an alien world.<br /> <br /> 6. Eco-Terrorism. I'll admit. I like the Captain Planet aspect of the game. Sometimes you want to play a game where you know who the enemy is. I like going out and just killing the bastards that fuck up the world.<br /> <br /> 7. Glasswalkers. I love this splat so much. Forward thinking, hacker Werewolves with Guns? Yes, please. The only White Wolf splat I love more is Sidereals from Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:26:16-08:00","id":1051673,"title":"","content":"Well, as they say, 'haters have to hate.' I think the problem that most people have with WtA is that the Garou (and Fera) are the closest thing to actual heroes in cWoD, despite their many flaws. They actually care, as a group, about the fate of the Earth and the fate of living entities (including living humans). <br /> <br /> What other group is motivated to care about the exploitation amd victimization of billions of humans? Every form of exploitation and victimization creates new Fomori, new Banes, and feeds the Wyrm. To make them out to be psychopaths is inaccurate and, quite frankly, misleading. The majority of Garou do not have high enough levels of Rage (6+) to be dangerous (Kindred are much more likely to frenzy than a Rage 5- Garou).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-19-2017, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:32:48-08:00","id":1051676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051673#post1051673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as they say, 'haters have to hate.' I think the problem that most people have with WtA is that the Garou (and Fera) are the closest thing to actual heroes in cWoD, despite their many flaws. They actually care, as a group, about the fate of the Earth and the fate of living entities (including living humans).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Since Garou are closer to &quot;heroes&quot; than other WoD gamelines, their flaws stand out more. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:40:02-08:00","id":1051679,"title":"","content":"To add to the &quot;ecoterrorism&quot; point not being exclusively a bad thing: One of the things the game has highlighted relatively well over the years is that the environment is danger and stopping it isn't simple. &quot;Captain Planet&quot; play can be both cathartic for those of us frustrated with it and looking for some escapist fantasy, as well as a spring board for the much more complicated issue that it isn't actually working. The Garou can't just kill pollution. Curbstomping some Pentex subsidiary's operation just means you stopped the worst of the worst polluters, and dozens of minor operations done by normal hard working people that aren't tools of a Wyrm cult are still doing what they do. One of the books even once had a side bar pointing out that they had tried to make a Pentex based oil company more hyperbolic <b>but they couldn't come up with a way to do so</b> because in reality it was already that stupidly bad.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty deep thing to consider. That a gaming book about a hyperbolic evil corporation that's purposefully doing all the horrible shit that most major corporations do out of willful ignorance in the name of profit had to throw up its hands and say, &quot;we couldn't come up with anything worse than this, what they're doing here is actually what real companies do.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:46:22-08:00","id":1051683,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Seems like a few folks in this thread could use a reminder of rule 3.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3. Respect other people\u2019s preferences. </span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It\u2019s fine to like or dislike certain aspects of our products, but not okay to get into hostile arguments over, for example, preferred editions of a game. This applies equally to non-Onyx or non-White Wolf games.</span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">If you don't like Werewolf the Apocalypse, that's fine, but don't come into a thread like this just to rant about what a terrible game you think it is. If you can't express your preferences respectfully, keep them to yourself.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:47:23-08:00","id":1051686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051673#post1051673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as they say, 'haters have to hate.' I think the problem that most people have with WtA is that the Garou (and Fera) are the closest thing to actual heroes in cWoD, despite their many flaws. They actually care, as a group, about the fate of the Earth and the fate of living entities (including living humans). <br /> <br /> What other group is motivated to care about the exploitation amd victimization of billions of humans? Every form of exploitation and victimization creates new Fomori, new Banes, and feeds the Wyrm. To make them out to be psychopaths is inaccurate and, quite frankly, misleading. The majority of Garou do not have high enough levels of Rage (6+) to be dangerous (Kindred are much more likely to frenzy than a Rage 5- Garou).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fera don't care about humanity. They only care about their spiritual &quot;ogus boogus&quot; that they need to keep in balance to order to keep the world in their divinely perfect order. They are not heroes, they are fanatical zealots, that's all. You'll find good heores and great villains amongst many Mages/Technocrats and changellings, and even wraiths, but werewolves are NOT heroes, they are just mere brutes. The ones that could be portrayed as heroes would be the Children of Gaia and the Keepers of the Inner Light (I think that's the name in english, I dunno), but the others are all a bunch of fascist assholes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:53:15-08:00","id":1051689,"title":"","content":"I at least respect the red talons - they are psychopats, sure, but at least they don't hide their true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:57:49-08:00","id":1051690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051676#post1051676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since Garou are closer to &quot;heroes&quot; than other WoD gamelines, their flaws stand out more. </div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what makes them compelling heroes. They are not Superman, they are Batman (Dark Knight). They are not the Avengers, they are the X-Men. While they are not anti-heroes, they are dark and tragic heroes who fight a seemingly hopeless fight not because they expect gratitude or reward, but because no one else is willing to step up to the plate as a group to save the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:58:09-08:00","id":1051691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051683#post1051683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Seems like a few folks in this thread could use a reminder of rule 3.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">If you don't like Werewolf the Apocalypse, that's fine, but don't come into a thread like this just to rant about what a terrible game you think it is. If you can't express your preferences respectfully, keep them to yourself.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Its not hostile argument about it. Unless it is expressly forbidden to have an opnion that may not agree with that of other people. I'm not saying people should dislike the game just as I do, I'm just saying the reasons why I don't. But, if having different tastes is offensive and forbidden, I'll say no more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:17:57-08:00","id":1051709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051691#post1051691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not hostile argument about it. Unless it is expressly forbidden to have an opnion that may not agree with that of other people. I'm not saying people should dislike the game just as I do, I'm just saying the reasons why I don't. But, if having different tastes is offensive and forbidden, I'll say no more</div> </div> </div> </div>You are welcome have any opinion you want. You are not welcome to publicly demean or insult those who do not share your opinion. Expressing dislike of a game is fine. Calling its fans fanatics is not.<br /> <br /> It's also against the forum rules to publicly dispute moderator action. If you have a problem with my warning, take it to the Contact Us link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:19:11-08:00","id":1051710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051709#post1051709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are welcome have any opinion you want. You are not welcome to publicly demean or insult those who do not share your opinion. Expressing dislike of a game is fine. Calling its fans fanatics is not.<br /> <br /> It's also against the forum rules to publicly dispute moderator action. If you have a problem with my warning, take it to the Contact Us link.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its all fine. No problem, I won't repeat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T19:53:37-08:00","id":1051821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051651#post1051651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 6. Eco-Terrorism. I'll admit. I like the Captain Planet aspect of the game. Sometimes you want to play a game where you know who the enemy is. I like going out and just killing the bastards that fuck up the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, Captain Planet strikes me as way more Mage in its approach than Werewolf. The &quot;Gaia&quot; that the group of five know is actually what they call their shared Avatar spirit. Problems are often waved away or produced without rhyme or reason, such as when some kind of pastiche gets used, often having to do with super-science gadgets. There's incredibly little that's visceral about it, even when using the title character as a deus ex machina. It's pretty much the case, or at least strongly seems to be, that people read &quot;Gaia&quot; and immediately jump to Ted Turner. I'd much prefer it if people jumped to God of War 2; it wouldn't be much better, but at least it would be a change of pace from the SAME THING THAT PEOPLE HAVE BEEN MEANINGLESSLY SHOUTING FOR TWENTY-FIVE YEARS.<br /> <br /> ...Pardon. I'm a bit sore over those points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T21:51:23-08:00","id":1051851,"title":"","content":"I have to agree. 'Captain Planet' should be considered to be a racial slur for Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T00:26:45-08:00","id":1051885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051679#post1051679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add to the &quot;ecoterrorism&quot; point not being exclusively a bad thing: One of the things the game has highlighted relatively well over the years is that the environment is danger and stopping it isn't simple. &quot;Captain Planet&quot; play can be both cathartic for those of us frustrated with it and looking for some escapist fantasy, as well as a spring board for the much more complicated issue that it isn't actually working. The Garou can't just kill pollution. Curbstomping some Pentex subsidiary's operation just means you stopped the worst of the worst polluters, and dozens of minor operations done by normal hard working people that aren't tools of a Wyrm cult are still doing what they do. One of the books even once had a side bar pointing out that they had tried to make a Pentex based oil company more hyperbolic <b>but they couldn't come up with a way to do so</b> because in reality it was already that stupidly bad.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty deep thing to consider. That a gaming book about a hyperbolic evil corporation that's purposefully doing all the horrible shit that most major corporations do out of willful ignorance in the name of profit had to throw up its hands and say, &quot;we couldn't come up with anything worse than this, what they're doing here is actually what real companies do.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, at times the 'lol captain planet' mentality can seem rather callous. After all, ecoterrorism being bad or not, enviroment and its state is a legitimate worry and we should be more aware of it. Dismissing garou because of that can easily be read as &quot;Being considerate about the enviroment is so 80s and lame&quot;, which..yeah.<br /> <br /> In general though, I'd say WtA's multiculturism can be a benefit if done right. Wendigo, Uktena, Stargazers and even Children of Gaia can add to a game if the players do their research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T03:50:02-08:00","id":1051927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051885#post1051885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general though, I'd say WtA's multiculturism can be a benefit if done right. Wendigo, Uktena, Stargazers and even Children of Gaia can add to a game if the players do their research.</div> </div> </div> </div>A-fucking-men. I would rather not shy away from portraying the suffering and sacrifices made by the indigenous people. I have learned so much about native culture researching my game. Assorted Comanche and Apache, Tonkawa, Karankawa, Cherokee, Caddo, Kickapoo, all of them have featured in the game in some capacity. There are so many distinct groups with their own languages, values and traditions. Exploring the issues of genocide and the westward expansion through the lens of WtA is a unique opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T05:39:16-08:00","id":1051955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051927#post1051927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A-fucking-men. I would rather not shy away from portraying the suffering and sacrifices made by the indigenous people. I have learned so much about native culture researching my game. Assorted Comanche and Apache, Tonkawa, Karankawa, Cherokee, Caddo, Kickapoo, all of them have featured in the game in some capacity. There are so many distinct groups with their own languages, values and traditions. Exploring the issues of genocide and the westward expansion through the lens of WtA is a unique opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone from a lesser known (white and well off, though) culture, yeah. WtA can easily be used to discuss colonialism and its results without guilt tripping the players. Shattered Dreams' historical sections are really neat on being clear what was wrong, but portraying the situation as complex.<br /> <br /> Heck, I currently play a Red Talon in a game. And discussion of radiation and how to combat it is..well..pretty sad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:40:26-08:00","id":1051978,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, I have used more real science in WtA games than I have in any other cWoD game (soft or hard). In the case of soft sciences, I have used anthropology, archeology, criminology, economic, sociology, etc. In the case of hard sciences, I have used biochemistry, climatology, ecology, genetics, geology, paleontology, physics, zoology, etc. I always think that people should come out of a WtA knowing more about the world than when they first came in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:38:14-08:00","id":1052114,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwann145</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture#post1051415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it relates to the overall &quot;World of Darkness&quot; anyway.<br /> \u200b\u2022The overall villain of the setting is the slow (or not so slow?) and subtle (or not so subtle?) corruption of the natural world, but you can't really do anything about it because the tribes just can't quit in-fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say this and is probably not the intended way but after the whole &quot;the complex technocracy was an accident&quot; i decided that author intent is not the way to go with any WoD/Chrod games.<br /> <br /> The superficial bad guy of Apocalypse is the wyrm/bsd but it isnt the complex/interesting bad guy of the setting. That is the Garou Nation itself.<br /> <br /> My analogy for werewolf is that its like the Walking dead with Negan. The series says to you that the bad guy are the zombies but the zombies arent really the compelling enemy or the main focus, they are a narrative tool. They are this unstoppable force that comes and forces the protagonist to cooperate and deal with morally questionable people in order to survive.<br /> <br /> Just like the garou the character\u00b4s goal is objectively good, survive for the human protagonist and save the world for the Garou. And yet they find themselves having to talk, negotiate and even compromise with people of questionable moral who, like them, have a objectively good goal (survive) but their methods are incredibly shady to say the least.<br /> <br /> So the Wyrm is the narrative excuse that force them to talk to the really compelling enemy Negan (the asshole tribes).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwann145</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture#post1051415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u2022There doesn't seem to be any &quot;personal horror&quot; in this game, as you have complete control of your character except for a frenzy, and unlike in VtM, frenzying isn't necessarily a bad thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frenzy aside i feel the true horror element of werewolf is compromise, how much you gonna let yourself go into this society to achieve what you want? Are you gonna defend equality for kinfolk and garous even when the system also exist in part to protect the kinfolks? Are you gonna take the life of baby metis black spiral dancer because she knows the location of the Sept? No? You gonna risk the lives of everyone for your conscience sake? Knowing that leaving her live is gonna add another one to the enemy numbers?<br /> <br /> You gonna live your life outside of the politics and shady deals? What if the kinfolk you love is about to married to another (and she/he doesn't want to) and you could win her/him back dueling the mate-to-be? Or negotiating your first son to the tribe of the kinfolk? Or worse negotiating your pack mate to another kinfolk<br /> <br /> Or what if a kinfolk comes from another sept hiding from her/his family? Would you fight them? Putting both septs at risk and knowing both could die just to prove a point? What happens if both die and there is no garou to fight the influence of pentex/the nearby hive?<br /> <br /> What if you could unite 3 warring Septs for the first time in generations if just that one mad elder got out of the way? The things 3 septs in concert could accomplish and all of that progress stopped by one asshole fianna.<br /> <br /> Are you gonna not fight and be a shame to your family? Most people dont care enough what their parent/grandfather think of them but here there is also the other way around, do you wanna be the reasons your son and grandsons and beyond have rough lives? Wanna live the rest of your life knowing your son/daughter thinks less of you because of the choices you make? Is the higher moral ground worth it?<br /> <br /> That for me is the horror of werewolf the decision you make and how seductive the garou society is for a garou. &quot;Be a good crusader, kill the wyrm and anything standing in your way and you will get honor, power and be a hero and be right....just dont think too much. Live fast and die young in the name of our war without changing a damn thing of this vicious circle and then an eternity in valhalla awaits you&quot; thats the speech of the garou nation at large. And the horror comes on how many garou buy it.<br /> <br /> Like a PC in a game said &quot;The problem with Garou society is that the garou are scare of living. Terrified of it. Thats why they throw their lives into glorious battles and give long winded song of dying with honor because that the easy way out. We fight, and we are damn good at it, and then in a moment we die and thats it, the problem that plague us are for the next generation to deal with. We did a &quot;good job&quot; and we punch out our ticket out and know that our ancestors and forebearers are proud of us and we can call it a good life.<br /> <br /> Because the alternative is living and living means we can fuck up. Having a kid and then dying in battle means we never have to find out if we could be good parents, means we will never face the fact that we suck at parenting or at our relationship. Means that we never have to face the fact that maybe we are fighting this war wrong and receive scorn from out septmates, tribemates or even packmates. It means we never have to see if we got what it takes to build instead of destroy. To look at our ancestors in the face and tell them &quot;NO, this is how we do things now&quot; and live with the consequences of that.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051625#post1051625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the one I considered the less profound of meaning, of mysticism, of substance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that the meaning of WtA is the one that is more relevant now than ever. The point of Werewolf is &quot;You might have the best of goals but that doesnt justify you&quot; and right now in this era of people arguing over important issues with the worse/morally questionable methods. Its being in a protest for the African-American Civil Rights Movement and see the black panthers protesting next to you, they got the same goals than you but not the same methods and you know that your cant really separate yourself from them because if the arent there you are even more alone in this fight.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051686#post1051686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fera don't care about humanity. They only care about their spiritual &quot;ogus boogus&quot; that they need to keep in balance to order to keep the world in their divinely perfect order. They are not heroes, they are fanatical zealots, that's all. You'll find good heores and great villains amongst many Mages/Technocrats and changellings, and even wraiths, but werewolves are NOT heroes, they are just mere brutes. The ones that could be portrayed as heroes would be the Children of Gaia and the Keepers of the Inner Light (I think that's the name in english, I dunno), but the others are all a bunch of fascist assholes</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but your argument is hypocritical at best. Lets take your pick of true &quot;heroes and great villains&quot; on mage because frankly i dont know anything about changeling. You are attributing them complexity and personalities beyond their faction while doing the opposite with the tribes.<br /> <br /> You are are implying that the mages can be more than their stereotype of wiccan verbena or unredeamable black hat technocrat which they are but then saying werewolves arent the same, that all members of the Get of Fenrir act/think the same. That a false equivalence. Or you are poorly informed and are comparing the 1st edition blurbs for the tribes with the late 2nd/revised factions of mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051651#post1051651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Politics. I like Werewolf politics better than Vampire politics because Garou argue about how to go about saving the Gaia from the Wyrm rather than backstab their fellow sept members due to self interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, the politics in werewolf unlike the ones in Vampire are generational. The deals you cut today are gonna affect not just you but your son and grandson. While at the same time the things you have to deal today are the result of deals your ancestor cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-20-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:06:27-08:00","id":1052133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052114#post1052114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> -a bunch of cool stuff-</div> </div> </div> </div><i>This guy groks werewolf. </i><br /> <br /> This bit in particular sticks out:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052114#post1052114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Like a PC in a game said &quot;The problem with Garou society is that the garou are scare of living. Terrified of it. Thats why they throw their lives into glorious battles and give long winded song of dying with honor because that the easy way out. We fight, and we are damn good at it, and then in a moment we die and thats it, the problem that plague us are for the next generation to deal with. We did a &quot;good job&quot; and we punch out our ticket out and know that our ancestors and forebearers are proud of us and we can call it a good life.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the members of my player's pack is tempted by this, but I hadn't thought about it in the way you describe until now. He is reckless to the point of self-destruction, and I think I know why, thanks to you. Death is certainly one way to hide from the cares of the world...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:18:39-08:00","id":1052220,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, I never had problems with my Fera PCs being suicidal and reckless. They want to raise their children, but they are willing to sacrifice themselves for the sake of the world. If they were not willing to risk their lives on a daily basis, the world would be overrun by Fomori.<br /> <br /> Compare the Fera to the rest of the supernatural creatures of cWoD. Kindred and KJ will do anything to live for centuries, Changelings and Mages try to avoid challenging fights whenever possible, and Wraiths do not usually care. The average Fera probably destroys a few dozen Fomori every year, meaning that the Fera probably destroy an average of a few million Fomori every year, and the Fomori are the least of the creatures that the Fera destroy to preserve the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:25:27-08:00","id":1052257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052114#post1052114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAwesome Loki stuff about Werewolf</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be the single greatest explanation of Werewolf that I've ever seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:11:55-08:00","id":1052506,"title":"","content":"&gt;This <b>is </b>the single greatest explanation of Werewolf that <b>anyone </b>has ever seen.<br /> Fixed that for you<br /> <br /> Actually Loki's mind altering explanation reminds me very much of the 'Choose Life' rant from Trainspotting 2.<br /> <br /> It's a work of genius Loki and has completely rewritten my view of Werewolf and how it should be played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 02-21-2017, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T06:51:46-08:00","id":1052542,"title":"","content":"The problem with comparing the Wyrm to a zombie plague is that the agents of the Wyrm can be clever while the victims of a zombie plague are brainless. Infernal Sorcerers can hide the evidence of their association with the Wyrm from Garou for months or years, helping them against dozens or hundreds of foes, before disappearing with a dozen Kinfolk children in the middle of the night (or otherwise betraying the Garou for their Demonic Lords). Even Fomori can be intelligent and subtle, allowing them to be quite effective, though the majority of them are animals and humans meant to spread misery and torment throughout the world through physical violence and sexual violation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:17:11-08:00","id":1052617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051632#post1051632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fomori and other Wyrm-crap are utter villains, Garou and Fera are the heroes. Very black and white. Have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part about Garou and Fera has already been covered, but I'm going to go ahead and chime in a rebuttal of the former point. I'm not saying the Wyrm is secretly the good guy or anything like that, but personally I find Fomori to be one of the more interestingly conceived and compelling antagonists in the WoD. Not everyone handles them this way, but a point that shows up more than once is that Fomori are still people. They've been physically, mentally, and spiritually corrupted, but still people. Sometimes this corruption is by choice or because of irredeemable character flaws, other times because of more subtle and human flaws that grew out of control, sometimes even by accident or coercion. What's worse is that they often have little recourse available for their condition. Fomori don't have much in the way of an organized society or support group outside of Wyrm cults and Pentex, which have a vested interest in exploiting and debasing them. Werewolves might conceivably help purge them of their corruption, but they're just as likely to kill them first. Other supernaturals, if they can even find them, tend to find them loathsome either out of physical revulsion or because the lore they have about them reinforces the idea that they are tainted and unclean. So the only thing left for them to do is either feed their flaws until they burn out in blaze of pus and balefire or eck out a solitary and wretched existence of rude survival while their disease slowly destroys them. <br /> <br /> I love Fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:26:15-08:00","id":1052776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052542#post1052542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with comparing the Wyrm to a zombie plague is that the agents of the Wyrm can be clever while the victims of a zombie plague are brainless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are miss-interpreting what i wrote, i never said that the Wyrm is brainless and cant be clever. I said that it serves the same narrative purpose as the zombies, that role being a objectively bad and disposable enemy that forces the tribes to cooperate and such makes the interactions between good tribes and morally questionable tribe members one not inherently violent.<br /> <br /> The complain of the wyrm being an irredeemable black hat enemy with no redeeming quality/complexities (for the most part) is accurate but incomplete. While the wyrm is that, its also needs to be that so as to serve the narrative of the game and make the true complex antagonist possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-21-2017, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:35:51-08:00","id":1052840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051632#post1051632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fomori and other Wyrm-crap are utter villains, Garou and Fera are the heroes. Very black and white. Have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at my thread on how Garou and Fera could very easily be awful monsters, if you're interested in bursting that bubble.<br /> <br /> And even from a Werewolf player perspective (mine is a controversial view, this is more mainstream) Garou literally started a Genocide of the other Fera. The War of Rage doesn't line up with your belief that the Garou and the Fera are the heroes. The Ravens sold out their friends and allies out of cowardice, they delivered messages between war-packs and watched from afar while the kinfolk of the Bears, Bulls and Boars were slaughtered. They shed no tears for the Bats. Then we have the Weresnakes, the Wererats, the Werehyenas and other nasties. And then we have the Ananasi, who are a big complicated grey area. Balance, on their terms, done their way. The arrogance.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is only black and white if you glance at it and squint. If you glance and squint at Vampire, the Anarchs are the good guys and the Sabbat are the bad guys. Hurray. Have fun. Except the Anarchs caused the 2008 financial crash just to bring down a few Princes and make a point about the power of Techno-Thaumaturgy, and the Sabbat are surprisingly champions of racial equality.<br /> <br /> Mage is black and white if you squint at it. Traditions are the good guys, Technocracy are the bad guys. Have fun. But you know that isn't true. Show the game line respect if you're going to comment on it. My views go against the grain but I do my research and I show my working. You're just saying &quot;lol it's all black and white lol&quot;. Big difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:24:10-08:00","id":1052927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Take a look at my thread on how Garou and Fera could very easily be awful monsters, if you're interested in bursting that bubble.<br /> <br /> And even from a Werewolf player perspective (mine is a controversial view, this is more mainstream) Garou literally started a Genocide of the other Fera. The War of Rage doesn't line up with your belief that the Garou and the Fera are the heroes. The Ravens sold out their friends and allies out of cowardice, they delivered messages between war-packs and watched from afar while the kinfolk of the Bears, Bulls and Boars were slaughtered. They shed no tears for the Bats. Then we have the Weresnakes, the Wererats, the Werehyenas and other nasties. And then we have the Ananasi, who are a big complicated grey area. Balance, on their terms, done their way. The arrogance.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is only black and white if you glance at it and squint. If you glance and squint at Vampire, the Anarchs are the good guys and the Sabbat are the bad guys. Hurray. Have fun. Except the Anarchs caused the 2008 financial crash just to bring down a few Princes and make a point about the power of Techno-Thaumaturgy, and the Sabbat are surprisingly champions of racial equality.<br /> <br /> Mage is black and white if you squint at it. Traditions are the good guys, Technocracy are the bad guys. Have fun. But you know that isn't true. Show the game line respect if you're going to comment on it. My views go against the grain but I do my research and I show my working. You're just saying &amp;quot;lol it's all black and white lol&amp;quot;. Big difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not just saying just for saying. It doesn't matter if the Fera and Garou specifically have flaws. They are still &quot;the good guys&quot;. Vampires don't have &quot;gentle monsters&quot;. They are either a fraud, a facade, the mask, or they are inhuman fiends. Anti-heroes at best, monstruous villains at worse. Mages are very hard to define. Both Traditions and Technocracy have what it takes to be heroes, anti heroes and villains. But Garou and Fera, no matter how bad they are, have a mission, and they face an utter evil. With vampires and Mages, it really is a matter of a point of view. Who is truly ideologically right? Should the kindred be free, as the anarchs say? Should the hierarchy and age be respected to keep order in the kindred's ancient society, like says the Camarilla? Or, trying to hold on to a fake humanity is stupid, and the kindred should actually embrace their true nature? About Mages, what is best? Safety or freedom? Were the Traditions neglecting their dude towards the sleepers? Is the Union opressive towards the masses? Has the Union improved the lifes of the human race? Do the Traditions keep the spark of creation alive?<br /> <br /> Both in Mage and Vampire, your enemy is not that different from you. You can even relate to them... Actually, they may even be right, and you wrong.<br /> <br /> But in WtA, the enemy has nothing on you. It's just madness and utter destruction, without any redeemable qualities. If you start &quot;seing things their way&quot;, it simply means that you have gone mad.<br /> <br /> It's like fighting nazis; it's a recurrent theme, because it is two dimensional - nazis are evil, and that's it. Defeat them at any costs, because they can't be resoaned with nor can you have any kind of diplomacy. No quarters, no mercy. That view IS black and white. Sorry, but I'm not sorry. You may not like my opinion, but you may not claim it's just an opinion of ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:39:41-08:00","id":1052961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Take a look at my thread on how Garou and Fera could very easily be awful monsters, if you're interested in bursting that bubble.</div> </div> </div> </div>From previous posts, he doesn't like WtA and greatly misunderstands the setting, so arguing against him on this is funny to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> TAnd even from a Werewolf player perspective (mine is a controversial view, this is more mainstream) Garou literally started a Genocide of the other Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement isn't entirely true. The Garou &quot;won&quot; against the other Fera, but that doesnt mean they started it. I want to say the Nagah book claims to have started it, in an effrt to knock the Garou down from their high horse. They just underestimated how good the Garou actually are at their jobs. Also, I don't think it was a true war. There have been a few threads on the War of Rage and what it was actually like. I think it's far more likely it was a series of long skirmishes that in retrospect was termed a &quot;war&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The War of Rage doesn't line up with your belief that the Garou and the Fera are the heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't necessarily take away from it either though. Your are talking about a &quot;war&quot; that happened (at least) several thousand years ago. A people can still be heroic, even if they have a dark past. Look at every human civilization ever. They can still have heroes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Ravens sold out their friends and allies out of cowardice, they delivered messages between war-packs and watched from afar while the kinfolk of the Bears, Bulls and Boars were slaughtered.</div> </div> </div> </div> It might have been cowardice. Or it was the only way they saw for them to survive. Either way, the Corax aren't typically looked at as &quot;heroes&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They shed no tears for the Bats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proof?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then we have the Weresnakes, the Wererats, the Werehyenas and other nasties. And then we have the Ananasi, who are a big complicated grey area. Balance, on their terms, done their way. The arrogance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Arrogance disqualifies someone from being a hero. I agree it isn't a great trait. But most &quot;heroes&quot; are in fact arrogant to some degree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052840#post1052840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Werewolf is only black and white if you glance at it and squint. If you glance and squint at Vampire, the Anarchs are the good guys and the Sabbat are the bad guys. Hurray. Have fun. Except the Anarchs caused the 2008 financial crash just to bring down a few Princes and make a point about the power of Techno-Thaumaturgy, and the Sabbat are surprisingly champions of racial equality.<br /> <br /> Mage is black and white if you squint at it. Traditions are the good guys, Technocracy are the bad guys. Have fun. But you know that isn't true. Show the game line respect if you're going to comment on it. My views go against the grain but I do my research and I show my working. You're just saying &quot;lol it's all black and white lol&quot;. Big difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was being patronizing of the Werewolf game. I honestly don't know why he's bothered to weight in on the topic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:50:39-08:00","id":1052995,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052927#post1052927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not just saying just for saying. It doesn't matter if the Fera and Garou specifically have flaws. They are still &quot;the good guys&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what context your refer that the garou are the &quot;good guys&quot;? In narrative of the game, of the setting or themselves?<br /> <br /> If you mean the Garou are good games by the narrative of the game then its iffy, while the game does says that you, the player, are the ones who gotta fight the wyrm the books never shy away from showing how the garou creates many of the problem they face today, arent as infalible as they believe themselves to be and lastly sometimes they arent that different from what they fight.<br /> <br /> You mean by the setting itself? Werewolf setting is ripe with examples of the garou nation being the worst enemy of the garou nation. And the setting present a society that sets the garous as heroes and the abuses and pressures that comes with it. They can be heroes despite their flaws, but those flaws (both internal and external) need to be overcome for them to be heroes. Or maybe they dont but they still manage to be heroes but grey ones.<br /> <br /> You mean themselves? Sure, the garou nation has a party line of them being the righteous warrior of mother gaia. The camarilla has a party line too, so does the traditions and while OOC and sometimes IC we know thats not as true as they present themselves, the party line IS there and IS enforced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052927#post1052927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't have &quot;gentle monsters&quot;. They are either a fraud, a facade, the mask, or they are inhuman fiends. Anti-heroes at best, monstruous villains at worse. Mages are very hard to define. Both Traditions and Technocracy have what it takes to be heroes, anti heroes and villains. But Garou and Fera, no matter how bad they are, have a mission, and they face an utter evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>And does the fact that they face utter evil as their mission justify them? Does that make them heroes just by dint of fighting the wyrm? Even if a werewolf abuses his mate, the same act that creates banes, is he still a hero? Or does the garou society consider him a hero?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052927#post1052927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With vampires and Mages, it really is a matter of a point of view. Who is truly ideologically right? Should the kindred be free, as the anarchs say? Should the hierarchy and age be respected to keep order in the kindred's ancient society, like says the Camarilla? Or, trying to hold on to a fake humanity is stupid, and the kindred should actually embrace their true nature? About Mages, what is best? Safety or freedom? Were the Traditions neglecting their dude towards the sleepers? Is the Union oppressive towards the masses? Has the Union improved the lifes of the human race? Do the Traditions keep the spark of creation alive?</div> </div> </div> </div>And those are compelling question that those games ask since 2nd edition and they make the games shine for it but how are those questions different from this ones?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052114#post1052114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> You gonna live your life outside of the politics and shady deals? What if the kinfolk you love is about to married to another (and she/he doesn't want to) and you could win her/him back dueling the mate-to-be? Or negotiating your first son to the tribe of the kinfolk? Or worse negotiating your pack mate to another kinfolk<br /> <br /> Or what if a kinfolk comes from another sept hiding from her/his family? Would you fight them? Putting both septs at risk and knowing both could die just to prove a point? What happens if both die and there is no garou to fight the influence of pentex/the nearby hive?<br /> <br /> What if you could unite 3 warring Septs for the first time in generations if just that one mad elder got out of the way? The things 3 septs in concert could accomplish and all of that progress stopped by one asshole fianna.<br /> <br /> Are you gonna not fight and be a shame to your family? Most people dont care enough what their parent/grandfather think of them but here there is also the other way around, do you wanna be the reasons your son and grandsons and beyond have rough lives? Wanna live the rest of your life knowing your son/daughter thinks less of you because of the choices you make? Is the higher moral ground worth it?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052927#post1052927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both in Mage and Vampire, your enemy is not that different from you. You can even relate to them... Actually, they may even be right, and you wrong.<br /> <br /> But in WtA, the enemy has nothing on you. It's just madness and utter destruction, without any redeemable qualities. If you start &quot;seing things their way&quot;, it simply means that you have gone mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the compelling enemy, the garou nation, does have a lot on you. They are your septmates, tribemates or even packmates that just bought to much of the Garou nation narrative. They want the same thing as you &quot;defeat the wyrm&quot; but then the problems starts.<br /> <br /> Is the treatment of the metis right? Are they soldier for gaia like the rest and the garou nation is being blind to their potential? Or are they dangerous for they might fail at a crucial moment because of their flaw/upbringing? Or allowing them in is gonna alienate the other tribes or condone their making? Can the other tribes change their outlook on them? Is worth the effort?<br /> <br /> The stated enemy is one, is as irredeamable as one can be, faceless and endless. But fighting that enemy is were the complex enemy get on you. When you start questioning your morals in the face of a war, from the approach to the old question of &quot;moral high ground vs practicality/realism&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052927#post1052927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not like my opinion, but you may not claim it's just an opinion of ignorance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well i suggested that your knowledge of the Werewolf came from 1st edition. Is not so much ignorance as lack of interest, and no one could blame you if way back when you picked up a copy of Apocalypse 1st, read it and got your opinions of the game from there and never read anything else. You like what you like and thats fine.<br /> <br /> However, i can point out your argument is setting a double standard. You are attributing a deepness to the other lines that didnt came from 1st ed while at the same time using the 1st ed interpretation of the werewolf. As i point out you are using the deep moral question the other 2 lines present while ignore the ones werewolf present. And finally you are comparing the antagonist in false equivalency.<br /> <br /> As a said before, i agree with the assessment that the Wyrm is a black/white enemy but thats a incomplete assessment of the antagonist of the game and fails to understand the narrative purpose of them. In mage terms, it would be like saying that that antagonist of mage are bad because the nephandi are unredeamable black hats<br /> <br /> Though as a side note i am curious what @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12985-schwann145\">Schwann145</a></b> thinks about this discussion and if any of the posters here has help him wrap his head around the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-21-2017, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T21:48:09-08:00","id":1053037,"title":"","content":"I think the concept that garou are monsters because their ancestors were cruel and such undercuts not only the present day garou, but also any other supernatural with a shady past.<br /> <br /> I mean, a Tzimisce who has taken an area of the slum as their own domain and makes sure the people are surviving may not do it from entirely altruistic reasons, but they still want to make sure their chosen people are all right. Might be that they themselves came from there and so the place is 'home' in a literal sense. To the people this vampire protects, they are a hero.<br /> <br /> Or an NWO agent who has a family and so she works twice as hard to make sure her daughter is safe.<br /> <br /> Just because these two are from the accepted antagonist splats, doesn't mean they cannot be heroes in a sense. Very much same with garou, looking at them as people rather than as a great whole is my preferred method of viewning WtA. Some Black Furies sacrifice men to this day for power, some Children of Gaia want the Nation under their control. Yet some Shadow Lords take great pains to right the wrongs of their past, such as the death of the Camazotz, and some Fenrir make it their live's work to fight against neo-nazism in the name of all skinheads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T22:46:52-08:00","id":1053059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052995#post1052995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Though as a side note i am curious what @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12985-schwann145\">Schwann145</a></b> thinks about this discussion and if any of the posters here has help him wrap his head around the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think I have a much better view of the game now and I'm enjoying the ongoing discussions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200bI will say though that I still don't see the personal horror of W:tA. For instance, your earlier examples are great story hooks but aren't intrinsic to the game itself and could easily be shared in any game really.<br /> \u200bCompare to Vampire: Regardless of where the story in a game is going or what you're doing in said story, there is always the underlying struggle of maintaining your humanity in the face of this beast that gets a slightly firmer grip of you as time goes on, every time you're forced to feed to sustain yourself, etc. With Mage, it's less intense of a struggle but there is still a very real concern about Paradox and every use of your powers, if you aren't careful and calculated enough, could cause backlash and have any number of severe and unexpected consequences to yourself or those around you.<br /> I don't see that system existing in Werewolf. Maybe I'm just missing it?<br /> <br /> \u200bI do really like the Zombie analogy though. That kinda makes things &quot;click&quot; into perspective; the Wyrm being the obvious villainous force but not necessarily the point of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12985-schwann145","name":"Schwann145","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T23:31:58-08:00","id":1053067,"title":"","content":"Hey Schwann145, <br /> <br /> I can't give you any first hand experience with the game since I have none myself, but a good friend of mine gave a really good explanation about WtA when I asked him similar questions to what you're asking now, primarily the personal horror part, and will do my best to repeat what he told me as accurately as I can:<br /> <br /> &quot;The personal horror in Werewolf the Apocolypse comes from being born as a Garu, and all that it entails. It means having a normal life up until a certain point where everything changes and suddenly you must pick a side in a conflict that's been going on since the Dawn of Time. It's about having a war against a cosmic force so ingrained into a culture that you're suddenly expected to accept and join, with the consiquences of not meaning death or worse. It's about adjusting to your transformation, going from either human or wolf to something in between and forever after being connected but separate from both worlds. It's about one day having a veil lifted from your eyes and suddenly being able to see the real consiquences of people's actions and how they breed gods and monsters beyond the wall that separates the spirit realm from the world you were born into. It's about looking up into the night sky and screaming because of the absolutely f$&amp;ked situation you've been born into and which you are expected to not only contribute too but also intentionally sire new recruits for who will have to undergo the same shit as you when you inevitably fall in a war that will last until the End of Time.&quot;<br /> - A Wise Storyteller; told to a WtA hater who then at last understood why WtA was one of the seminal tabletop RPGs of it's time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope that helps, it certainly did for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 02-22-2017, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T06:33:00-08:00","id":1053161,"title":"","content":"And to realize that you cannot give up because no one else is willing to fight. The Garou are tragic heroes because, unlike mortals, they cannot escape into the comfort of insanity when they are forced to witness unspeakable horrors. And Garou will witness unspeakable horrors because they will follow Bane and Fomori to the source, whether it is a Fortune 500 company, a child brothel, a death camp, a Fomori family, a lair of a serial killer, etc. And, on occasion, Garou will have to choose between two bad choices because no one else is willing to make the choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:01:36-08:00","id":1053172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwann145</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053059#post1053059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think I have a much better view of the game now and I'm enjoying the ongoing discussions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200bI will say though that I still don't see the personal horror of W:tA. For instance, your earlier examples are great story hooks but aren't intrinsic to the game itself and could easily be shared in any game really.<br /> \u200bCompare to Vampire: Regardless of where the story in a game is going or what you're doing in said story, there is always the underlying struggle of maintaining your humanity in the face of this beast that gets a slightly firmer grip of you as time goes on, every time you're forced to feed to sustain yourself, etc. With Mage, it's less intense of a struggle but there is still a very real concern about Paradox and every use of your powers, if you aren't careful and calculated enough, could cause backlash and have any number of severe and unexpected consequences to yourself or those around you.<br /> I don't see that system existing in Werewolf. Maybe I'm just missing it?<br /> <br /> \u200bI do really like the Zombie analogy though. That kinda makes things &quot;click&quot; into perspective; the Wyrm being the obvious villainous force but not necessarily the point of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Werewolf doesn't bill itself as &quot;a storytelling game of personal horror&quot; and makes no directed attempts to be one, so it's not going to be too terribly obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:14:44-08:00","id":1053177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwann145</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053059#post1053059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bI will say though that I still don't see the personal horror of W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that it matters much but...that wasn't the tag line of Werewolf. &quot;Personal horror&quot; was the tag line of Vampire.<br /> <br /> Vampire: A Storytelling Game of Personal Horror<br /> Werewolf: A Storytelling Game of Savage Horror<br /> Mage: A Storytelling Game Of Modern Magick<br /> <br /> ...and so on.<br /> <br /> There can be plenty to be found (as shown earlier), but you generally have to look for it since &quot;personal horror&quot; isn't central to the game's themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:17:35-08:00","id":1053181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1052927#post1052927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't have &quot;gentle monsters&quot;. They are either a fraud, a facade, the mask, or they are inhuman fiends. Anti-heroes at best, monstruous villains at worse.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not if you're playing a Child of Osiris or a Golconda campaign.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:51:10-08:00","id":1053207,"title":"","content":"Or even a high Humanity Anarch or Camarilla game. The only Kindred that are required to be monsters are the Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:52:33-08:00","id":1053208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053181#post1053181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not if you're playing a Child of Osiris or a Golconda campaign.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or, for a different form of vampire, Flame of the Rising Phoenix. They even have the advantage of being able to seal away their powers and walk around as, essentially, a normal human for a day, but it's very demanding and requires two basically double-priced Disciplines both at four dots. KotE really gouges you with the xp prices...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:55:45-08:00","id":1053210,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I do find it odd that KJ Disciplines cost so much when they do not offer any real advantages. In my games, I just make the cost the same as the Kindred Disciplines for Caitiff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:30:34-08:00","id":1053226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053172#post1053172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Werewolf doesn't bill itself as &quot;a storytelling game of personal horror&quot; and makes no directed attempts to be one, so it's not going to be too terribly obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053177#post1053177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that it matters much but...that wasn't the tag line of Werewolf. &quot;Personal horror&quot; was the tag line of Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSee, here I thought it was a tagline for WoD in general. Explains why I wasn't finding that theme!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12985-schwann145","name":"Schwann145","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:44:52-08:00","id":1053352,"title":"","content":"Yeah, WtA is more a game of Lovecraftian horror (corruption, insanity, and Things Man Was Not Meant to Know) than a game of personal horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T12:16:16-08:00","id":1053363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053207#post1053207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or even a high Humanity Anarch or Camarilla game. The only Kindred that are required to be monsters are the Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the Baali don't need to be Monsters. A Third of them are trying to stop the end of the world at the hands of Demons, and they're pragmatic enough to sacrifice a few school buses full of children to do it.<br /> <br /> For irredeemable Monsters, you'll be looking at certain Paths, truly Infernalist Vampires, lower Humanity Vampires, serial Diablerists... I'd argue that the Sabbat are primarily monsters, since they are performative edgy Frat-bros who are SO over humanity that they drink people dry to make a point about how little they care. Every thread with &quot;oh, but when you think about it, aren't the Camarilla and the Sabbat equally bad?&quot;, and people sit there and nod along until someone points out &quot;no, no they definitely aren't, what are you talking about.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2017, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:26:20-08:00","id":1053418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053161#post1053161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to realize that you cannot give up because no one else is willing to fight. The Garou are tragic heroes because, unlike mortals, they cannot escape into the comfort of insanity when they are forced to witness unspeakable horrors. And Garou will witness unspeakable horrors because they will follow Bane and Fomori to the source, whether it is a Fortune 500 company, a child brothel, a death camp, a Fomori family, a lair of a serial killer, etc. And, on occasion, Garou will have to choose between two bad choices because no one else is willing to make the choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...that's not quite...I mean you could look at it like...well...ok, I actually have a small problem with this line of thinking.<br /> <br /> As noble and well intentioned as it is, there is a serious danger to seeing the werewolf condition in Apocalypse as that. Because 1) werewolves aren't the only people who are willing to take action about situations like that, human beings fight all the time against the Wyrm without even realizing it and despite being woefully outmatched, and the idea that the Garu are the only ones willing stems more from Garu tradition/propaganda and the second point. 2) The Garu know that they're some of the most potent killing machines on the planet and therefore they adopt ideas like this to justify their actions, and that has led to a majority of the atrocities the Garu nation's commuted across history. <br /> <br /> Another way to look at this is the super hero fallacy: Who does more good? A superhero, or a social worker? Sure, one can leap over building in a single bound and fight cosmic evil without being driven insane or being, what scientists officially call, &quot;super killed.&quot; But a superhero's purpose in comics and literature is to battle and stop threats that are beyond the human ken, and inspire people to do good in their own way within the context of their own lives.<br /> <br /> I know that analogy isn't perfect for the Garu, but this notion that only the Garu can save the world crops up again and again. And I think this is on purpose to let the audience question whether this is true, or just more of that cultural inheritance that so defines the existence of most Garu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 02-22-2017, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:44:35-08:00","id":1053428,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends. Who else is equipped to deal with combat oriented Fomori? The average functional Fomori created with Possessed will likely be built with 25 Power Points, meaning that the combat oriented Fomori will be coming in with combat capabilities that butcher an entire infantry platoon. The Fera probably kill around 3 million Fomori every year, so humanity would probably have to be willing to lose 60 million troops a year to kill off the Fomori (assuming only half of the Fomori are combat capable). Of course, these are only my estimates, but I have never seen a WtA campaign where the players were not forced to butcher an average of a few dozen Fomori each. And we are not even talking about the Big Bads, which cannot be faced by mortal armies because of the terror that they cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:06:26-08:00","id":1053447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053428#post1053428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it depends. Who else is equipped to deal with combat oriented Fomori? The average functional Fomori created with Possessed will likely be built with 25 Power Points, meaning that the combat oriented Fomori will be coming in with combat capabilities that butcher an entire infantry platoon. The Fera probably kill around 3 million Fomori every year, so humanity would probably have to be willing to lose 60 million troops a year to kill off the Fomori (assuming only half of the Fomori are combat capable). Of course, these are only my estimates, but I have never seen a WtA campaign where the players were not forced to butcher an average of a few dozen Fomori each. And we are not even talking about the Big Bads, which cannot be faced by mortal armies because of the terror that they cause.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...*takes a long and deep breath while remembering what his friend taught him about the game*......ok, let me put this another way. <br /> <br /> If it was simply a matter about numbers and destroying the servants of the Wyrm, then why hasn't the Garu nation defeated the Wyrm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:17:38-08:00","id":1053459,"title":"","content":"Personal Horror it should be noted was the Vampire The Masquerade tagline. Werewolf the Apocalypse was always tagged Savage Horror. With that said the personal horror of Werewolf is easy enough to discover. The first case lies in Rage. To demonstrate I shall paraphrase and reassemble from a few sources. <br /> <br /> First you have to understand what Rage is...<br /> <br /> Imagine the very angriest you have EVER been. In your life. That mindless, blinding fury that possesses a life of its own and forgoes all reason, that comes with screaming and tears and violence and a need to break something or make someone bleed. Congratulations you've just recalled something that is a tenth of Rage 1. That feeling that stirs beneath the surface of a Garou psyche. This is a weapon and a Curse as is covered by using Rage and the effects of the Curse as given in the rules. But let's expand it. Imagine family and friends, imagine the arguments and fallings out you have with them, imagine what happens when those same arguments can stir Rage, the same Rage that turns a Garou into a mindless nine foot tall killing machine in the throws of frenzy... What happens when you return to sense drenched in mothers blood? Or maybe you keep them safe, because there are other monsters out there who would harm them, use them, corrupt them? How free could they be? What rights do they have if they are part of Garou society? Or do you leave them forever if they are not? Can you afford to do so though? Gaia needs warriors and th Garou need support from those who can sits in the human societies of the world. <br /> Free they are an Achilles heel or utterly distanced. Guarded they become pet like. Useful they are servitors and fully equal they'll die on someone's claws. <br /> <br /> That's family and Kinfolk. Rage can lead to much of he intertribal strife too. <br /> <br /> Then there's the Litany. You suffer renown loss for breaking it. It's the Nations law to be upheld. How many bad things must you do to protect it? <br /> Good cops who discover the wrong thing at the wrong time? <br /> Honest free media who are going to print the wrong story?<br /> Packmate mates with another Garou? <br /> The list goes on and the Litany is full of laws that can make you face some very hard choices. <br /> <br /> Werewolf is a game of the line in the sand. It's a game of moments, desperate ones. It's a game where existence is on the line in a very real and visceral way. It's a game of fight or die, become wise or lose. It's a war of fang and claw and spirit and metaphor. It's the only battle left to fight and each hour could be the last hour of the last day and it could be your deeds that means it is not. And those deeds may be terrible and yet they prevent far worse. Do the ends justify the means? Or do they just feed the foe you face? <br /> <br /> In the end only one question remains to the Garou...<br /> When will you Rage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:23:27-08:00","id":1053464,"title":"","content":"Because it is literally impossible to destroy the Wyrm because you would be destroying the very concept of destruction. The Garou probably only kill a fifth of the Fomori killed by the Fera. Anyway, the Fera probably only kill three million Fomori per year, so the global population of Fomori continues to slowly grow despite the actions of the Fera.<br /> <br /> The only way to reduce the production of Fomori is to improve the human condition and the environment, but that is the paradox with current human populations. If you improve the human condition, you strengthen the Wyrm by destroying the environment. If you improve the environment, you strengthen the Wyrm by worsening the human condition. Without a stabilization in human populations, technology cannot catch up, so that is not a solution either. In effect, the Fera (and the world) are playing a game of 'heads I win, tails you lose' with the Wyrm, the the Wyrm being the con man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:21:14-08:00","id":1053493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051885#post1051885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, at times the 'lol captain planet' mentality can seem rather callous. After all, ecoterrorism being bad or not, enviroment and its state is a legitimate worry and we should be more aware of it. Dismissing garou because of that can easily be read as &quot;Being considerate about the enviroment is so 80s and lame&quot;, which..yeah.<br /> <br /> In general though, I'd say WtA's multiculturism can be a benefit if done right. Wendigo, Uktena, Stargazers and even Children of Gaia can add to a game if the players do their research.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to second this. Actually, what won me over back in the day for WtA was the whole environmentalism thing. It was just good to have a game with a non-human centered worldview with that theme. I actually missed from Forsaken some stronger connection between the Uratha and the natural world (and I actually liked Changing Breeds. Burn me.).<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;lol captain planet&quot; mentality always made me a bit angry in fact. As something like a game with the state of our world as a central theme would be laughable on itself. As if environmentalism would be laughable on itself. It just makes me angry and depressed the more I think about that reaction (and in fact, I could totally understand the garou, if not agreeing with all their methods and they actually have some really ugly sides I absolutely despise). Not long ago, we watched Before the Flood with one of my friends and seeing those pictures over one and a half hour got me into the perfect WtA mood, which is not exactly a merry thing.<br /> <br /> Yeah, my degree is in nature conservation engineering and this game had a part in me deciding to go for that instead history. Call me a filthy hippy if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-22-2017, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:50:23-08:00","id":1053507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053464#post1053464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it is literally impossible to destroy the Wyrm because you would be destroying the very concept of destruction. The Garou probably only kill a fifth of the Fomori killed by the Fera. Anyway, the Fera probably only kill three million Fomori per year, so the global population of Fomori continues to slowly grow despite the actions of the Fera.<br /> <br /> The only way to reduce the production of Fomori is to improve the human condition and the environment, but that is the paradox with current human populations. If you improve the human condition, you strengthen the Wyrm by destroying the environment. If you improve the environment, you strengthen the Wyrm by worsening the human condition. Without a stabilization in human populations, technology cannot catch up, so that is not a solution either. In effect, the Fera (and the world) are playing a game of 'heads I win, tails you lose' with the Wyrm, the the Wyrm being the con man.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Surely you must see the contradiction here? &quot;The Garu are the only ones who can stop the Wyrm, but the Wrym cannot be stopped&quot;, is one of the enormous fallacies of the game setting and is one of the big morals that Apocalypse is trying to teach. It's that in order to fight for humanity and the world you cannot have contempt for humanity and the world. And the Garu have loads of contempt, so much so that their most noble belief is built upon the notion that the humans cannot resist the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> ...rather than the truth, which is that the Garu made the Wyrm the greatest ally of humanity. The Wyrm is kind to those who serve it, it empowers them and allow them to fight creatures that are so impossibly more powerful than they are that their genetic memory screams in terror just at the sight of them. The fact that the greatest force of the Wyrm within the World of Darkness is a human run corporation is meant to showcase that it's not the Garu who will save the world. It's humanity. Humanity must learn to either co-exist on the planet in harmony with the environment, or it will destroy the planet and itself in time. Those are the only outcomes, because like you already stated, the Wyrm has stacked the deck against the other forces of the planet by playing upon their own contempt for humanity to the point where either humanity must free itself from the Wyrm, or the Wyrm WILL win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:07:51-08:00","id":1053777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schwann145</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053059#post1053059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have a much better view of the game now and I'm enjoying the ongoing discussions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200bI will say though that I still don't see the personal horror of W:tA. For instance, your earlier examples are great story hooks but aren't intrinsic to the game itself and could easily be shared in any game really.<br /> \u200bCompare to Vampire: Regardless of where the story in a game is going or what you're doing in said story, there is always the underlying struggle of maintaining your humanity in the face of this beast that gets a slightly firmer grip of you as time goes on, every time you're forced to feed to sustain yourself, etc. With Mage, it's less intense of a struggle but there is still a very real concern about Paradox and every use of your powers, if you aren't careful and calculated enough, could cause backlash and have any number of severe and unexpected consequences to yourself or those around you.<br /> I don't see that system existing in Werewolf. Maybe I'm just missing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally i am gonna quote Heavy arms here that put it better:<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051447#post1051447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? I mean, mechanically there's not that much &quot;personal horror&quot; in any of the WoD games. There is however plenty of potential for it even if most WtA games tend to go for the action horror angle instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>So no, mechanically there is very little that enforces &quot;personal horror&quot; in any wod games. Feeding can be made a chore with only dominate 1 or 2. And i have made a build for mage that render paradox almost toothless While i also gonna say that Paradox in my opinion is more of a mechanic to avoid to break the setting more than for personal horror but if you see it that way is good too. So Rage/delirium aside, mechanically, there isnt any inherent &quot;personal horror&quot;....mechanically though, the question i put forward arent just plot seed but inherent parts of the setting.<br /> <br /> Whatever personal horror there are is one that both the DM and Player bring to the table themselves. I think thats a good thing though, the key word in &quot;personal horror&quot; is personal in that it have to be tailor made for the situation, player and character and thats why i think Chrod fails with their &quot;one size fits all&quot; behavior meters and &quot;personal horror mechanics&quot; trying to standardize something that has to carefully constructed on case per case basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053428#post1053428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it depends. Who else is equipped to deal with combat oriented Fomori? The average functional Fomori created with Possessed will likely be built with 25 Power Points, meaning that the combat oriented Fomori will be coming in with combat capabilities that butcher an entire infantry platoon. The Fera probably kill around 3 million Fomori every year, so humanity would probably have to be willing to lose 60 million troops a year to kill off the Fomori (assuming only half of the Fomori are combat capable).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are too focused on number/stats. I really doesnt matter how many fomori the garou can or cant kill because they are just a symptoms of the problem. Sure the garou are the only ones willing and capable of facing monsters like a nexus crawler or a army of fomori but where they come from? What condition make their existence possible? Shouldnt the garou organize better and try to avoid the fomori army from forming or the nexus crawler from....crawling into reality instead of just concentrate on fighting it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053418#post1053418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to look at this is the super hero fallacy: Who does more good? A superhero, or a social worker? Sure, one can leap over building in a single bound and fight cosmic evil without being driven insane or being, what scientists officially call, &quot;super killed.&quot; But a superhero's purpose in comics and literature is to battle and stop threats that are beyond the human ken, and inspire people to do good in their own way within the context of their own lives.<br /> <br /> I know that analogy isn't perfect for the Garu, but this notion that only the Garu can save the world crops up again and again. And I think this is on purpose to let the audience question whether this is true, or just more of that cultural inheritance that so defines the existence of most Garu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously the answer is a Hero who is also a social worker :P<br /> <br /> Joking aside the analogy does fit the garou. Remembers me of a PC we had who was a social worker garou, and help a woman leave her abusive husband, it was a touching scene in which the woman break down saying that her children were asking for her dad and she didnt knew what to tell them with the garou telling her that the man is still their father so she shouldn't tell them to hate him but made them understand that he cant no longer be part of their family. While this happened of the packmembers keep suggesting to just go and tear the abuser husband to bits with the social worker saying no because the point was that the woman herself learned to stand on her feet or forever be under the abuser influence even if he is dead.<br /> <br /> A social worker that help a woman break the cycle of abuse and stops it from spreading for generations is doing more to combat the wyrm influence than killing 100 fomoris. Thats ties to my idea of the seductiveness of the garou nation.<br /> <br /> Had the social worked failed he would received scorn and a talk of &quot;you should have just killed the husband and avoid the banes situation you coward&quot; but had the garou ignore the woman and just head straight to fighting the banes the situation created and died without killing them all, then the garou nation would sing praises about how they lost another brave warrior. The garou society only treasures 1 kind of failure, the one resulting from violence, which in turn makes garou more willing to approach everything with it because win or loose they are still heroes. But with the other approachs they only are &quot;heroes&quot; if they win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053428#post1053428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, these are only my estimates, but I have never seen a WtA campaign where the players were not forced to butcher an average of a few dozen Fomori each. And we are not even talking about the Big Bads, which cannot be faced by mortal armies because of the terror that they cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have played a 3 years long game. On PBP (which means multiple scenes at the same time) taking a character from Cub all the way to anthro (rank 4) and we fought 1 fomori, 3 banes and 7 Black Spiral Dancers. And for a big event a nexus crawler and that was it. We, as players, just werent interested in fighting scores of fomori or banes. Sure the wyrm was there, the war informed the interactions of our characters and moral questions about it but i could argue that could have just handle the actual wyrm smashing out of camera and it would change very little. The journey to prepare to fight the wyrm was the meaty storylines, making pacts and alliances. Playing the diplomat or just witnessing truly horrendous sides to the garou nation and doing or not doing something about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053507#post1053507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely you must see the contradiction here? &quot;The Garu are the only ones who can stop the Wyrm, but the Wrym cannot be stopped&quot;, is one of the enormous fallacies of the game setting and is one of the big morals that Apocalypse is trying to teach. It's that in order to fight for humanity and the world you cannot have contempt for humanity and the world. And the Garu have loads of contempt, so much so that their most noble belief is built upon the notion that the humans cannot resist the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another way of looking at it is that the garou can never win but as long as they fight the wyrm will never win. That if Gaia created all fera with a purpose then the Garou are white cell to combat the infection of the wyrm but that the wyrm can never truly be gone so they will fight forever in a cycle. Even if they purify the wyrm and make it sane again along with the weaver they will always have to fight and die to maintain the balance. Everything they do dont matter but at the same times matter a lot and that their purpose was never to win but to fight the war endlessly but the war must be fought. I am not saying this is the right assumption but it is a way of looking at it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053418#post1053418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...that's not quite...I mean you could look at it like...well...ok, I actually have a small problem with this line of thinking.<br /> <br /> As noble and well intentioned as it is, there is a serious danger to seeing the werewolf condition in Apocalypse as that. Because 1) werewolves aren't the only people who are willing to take action about situations like that, human beings fight all the time against the Wyrm without even realizing it and despite being woefully outmatched, and the idea that the Garu are the only ones willing stems more from Garu tradition/propaganda and the second point. 2) The Garu know that they're some of the most potent killing machines on the planet and therefore they adopt ideas like this to justify their actions, and that has led to a majority of the atrocities the Garu nation's commuted across history.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053507#post1053507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...rather than the truth, which is that the Garu made the Wyrm the greatest ally of humanity. The Wyrm is kind to those who serve it, it empowers them and allow them to fight creatures that are so impossibly more powerful than they are that their genetic memory screams in terror just at the sight of them. The fact that the greatest force of the Wyrm within the World of Darkness is a human run corporation is meant to showcase that it's not the Garu who will save the world. It's humanity. Humanity must learn to either co-exist on the planet in harmony with the environment, or it will destroy the planet and itself in time. Those are the only outcomes, because like you already stated, the Wyrm has stacked the deck against the other forces of the planet by playing upon their own contempt for humanity to the point where either humanity must free itself from the Wyrm, or the Wyrm WILL win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally i think there is a middle ground to this in which the garou can do a lot to help humanity and free them from the wyrm but it must do so with hard work and hard decisions, the ones that might not necessarily include violence, there is a time and place for violence and such but also there is place to inspire or build lasting things that combat the wyrm influence on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-23-2017, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:33:26-08:00","id":1053946,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2179\" data-vbnamecard=\"2179\">LokiRavenSpeak</a>, I have heard few people sum up the essence of WtA better than you did right here. I tip my hat to you. <br /> <br /> Also, another acceptable answer is: The superhero's superpower is social working. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Corrections: mistook you for the King's Raven for a second 02-23-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:47:18-08:00","id":1053958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053777#post1053777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Joking aside the analogy does fit the garou. Remembers me of a PC we had who was a social worker garou, and help a woman leave her abusive husband, it was a touching scene in which the woman break down saying that her children were asking for her dad and she didnt knew what to tell them with the garou telling her that the man is still their father so she shouldn't tell them to hate him but made them understand that he cant no longer be part of their family. While this happened of the packmembers keep suggesting to just go and tear the abuser husband to bits with the social worker saying no because the point was that the woman herself learned to stand on her feet or forever be under the abuser influence even if he is dead.<br /> <br /> A social worker that help a woman break the cycle of abuse and stops it from spreading for generations is doing more to combat the wyrm influence than killing 100 fomoris. Thats ties to my idea of the seductiveness of the garou nation.<br /> <br /> Had the social worked failed he would received scorn and a talk of &quot;you should have just killed the husband and avoid the banes situation you coward&quot; but had the garou ignore the woman and just head straight to fighting the banes the situation created and died without killing them all, then the garou nation would sing praises about how they lost another brave warrior. The garou society only treasures 1 kind of failure, the one resulting from violence, which in turn makes garou more willing to approach everything with it because win or loose they are still heroes. But with the other approachs they only are &quot;heroes&quot; if they win.<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is super cool.<br /> <br /> just curious what were the demographics of the social worker garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:28:41-08:00","id":1053979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053958#post1053958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is super cool.<br /> <br /> just curious what were the demographics of the social worker garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>He started as volunteer in a battered women's shelter and a homeless shelter. It was volunteering the owner died. Then he step up and a full time employee while brokering deals with city spirits to protect the place.<br /> <br /> It was also a connection to a nearby bone gnawer community. I dont know if those were the demographics you were asking me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:42:22-08:00","id":1053985,"title":"","content":"I probably used the word wrong but what tribe and auspice was that character? Kind of reminds me of the fake preist CoG from the novel Wyrm wolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:32:37-08:00","id":1054016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053985#post1053985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably used the word wrong but what tribe and auspice was that character? Kind of reminds me of the fake preist CoG from the novel Wyrm wolf</div> </div> </div> </div>For what i remember the character started as Silver fang but for some OCC drama he got to switch tribe to Children of Gaia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:48:42-08:00","id":1054025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1053181#post1053181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not if you're playing a Child of Osiris or a Golconda campaign.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually played a game that I were seeking Golconda. And I can tell you, human morals are NOT a thing, even for Golconda. We were playing 4th generations, and my player started the road of Golconda. His view of the world was a fatalistic of nihiilism; he could watch as a Tzimisce twists and torture a mortal without blinking. Such a barbaric act for him was like a lion eating a zebra; mortals are born and die, either from hunger, disease, violence or age. The tzismisce is the real victim in such a picture actually; the mortal will reencarnate, or will go to the next stage, and will have a new chance in his life. But the Tzimisce pollute his soul by such acts. The most despicable evils are actually creatures of piety; powerful vampires, for example, live in constant paranoic fear, because their monstruous acts play against themselves. See? That's a Vampire with high levels of humanity, &quot;a Saint&quot;. However, he were still monstruous, for he had a strictly police of &quot;non interference&quot;, just like a naturalist watching a polar bear devouring a seal. He would watch a setite drink a baby dry, or torturing a pregnant woman with the same apathy and uninterest that he would see a bunch of hunters burning to death a Vampire that commited several atrocities.<br /> Oh, by the way, he were a Children of Osiris too.<br /> <br /> Vampires are monsters. The lot of them. They may disguise it and may even try to deny it or t\u00f4 fight against it, but in the end, that's what they truly are. At best, they'll have an alien mindset that aren't evil, but it's not also human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T14:54:39-08:00","id":1054029,"title":"","content":"And you were playing that character wrong because you would have bern forced to roll Conscience for every evil act witnessed. Your ST obviously did not understand the VtM morality system. If you witness evil and have the power to prevent that evil and you do nothing, it is an equivalent sin of Humanity. Otherwise, the Humanity system is meaningless because you could just have an understanding with a serial killer to supply you with the blood of his victims when he is done with raping and torturing them in exchange for using your powers to protect him from discovery by the authorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-23-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T15:42:41-08:00","id":1054053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054025#post1054025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually played a game that I were seeking Golconda. And I can tell you, human morals are NOT a thing, even for Golconda.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your personal, anecdotal evidence isn't proof of ALL vampires being monsters. Also, I was mainly referring to Humanity Golconda. I think you and the ST had a bad grasp on how Humanity and Golconda actually work. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires are monsters. The lot of them. They may disguise it and may even try to deny it or t\u00f4 fight against it, but in the end, that's what they truly are. At best, they'll have an alien mindset that aren't evil, but it's not also human. </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's just not accurate. Moral vampires can and do exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T16:04:10-08:00","id":1054065,"title":"","content":"I agree. It says in V20 (p. 312) that any Kindred with Humanity 8+ is more human than human. Since you have to be Humanity 7+ and Conscience 4+ to seek Golconda, Golconda seekers are objectively good people and are incapable of doing or tolerating evil actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T20:18:23-08:00","id":1054173,"title":"","content":"Is Saulot more human than humans?<br /> <br /> Old vampires are NOT humans. They are inhumans by nature, the way they see things is different from mortals. &quot;Tolerating evil actions&quot; is a matter of perspective. Siddarta Gautama (the Buddha), Jesus Christ and many, many others, could deal with evil in their own terms. Siddartha for example, would see his kingdom burn, without condemning the enemy nation that did, for understanding how violence is part of life. He abhored violence, but understands. Jesus knew that the romans were opressive, and yet he would say &quot;to Cesar what is of Cesar&quot;. By the same way, my character would be disgusted by by the barbaric acts of a Tzimisce, but he were an absolutely pacifist, and would never do a violent act, no matter under what circunstances, not even for self defense. So, seeing violence as the natural state of &quot;those inferior souls&quot; was the way of dealing with it.<br /> <br /> Even with humanity 10 (like my char was), he still had a beast inside of him. He still had to drink blood to live. He were still imortal, still a creature of the night, still dead<br /> <br /> Still inhuman","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T22:20:06-08:00","id":1054196,"title":"","content":"If you want to keep talking about your VtM character, please post him on the VtM forum. I am sure that the people there will have something to say. Since this is a WtA forum though, can we please talk about the topic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-24-2017, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T00:46:07-08:00","id":1054215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054196#post1054196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to keep talking about your VtM character, please post him on the VtM forum. I am sure that the people there will have something to say. Since this is a WtA forum though, can we please talk about the topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Yeah. Someone start a new thread so I can rant about the mental gymnastics one has to perform to think allowing someone to get tortured is AOK at Humanity 9-10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-24-2017, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T01:21:39-08:00","id":1054221,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let me make it official.<br /> <br /> Karlgust take the Vampire discussion to the VtM forum f you wish to discuss that game. Any more off topic posts or posts about how you dislike Apocalypse will be addressed appropriately up to and including suspension of posting privileges.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T01:43:37-08:00","id":1054228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054215#post1054215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Yeah. Someone start a new thread so I can rant about the mental gymnastics one has to perform to think allowing someone to get tortured is AOK at Humanity 9-10.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be interested in that as well, given the implications it has.<br /> <br /> In general,though, macro vs micro is something I'd recommend people to do in these threads. Gaia myth being a lie to these guys: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/916359-a-npc-antagonist-template-for-people-to-use\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-people-to-use</a> would be grand, because it would support their views. Even if it really isn't true, to the narrative of the Currs it justifies them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T06:31:59-08:00","id":1054281,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that the Currs would be considered a Mockery Breed under current WtA Lore, so I doubt that they would have a sufficient connection to the spirit world to understand how wrong they are about Gaia. However, the Currs are not a canon Fera Breed, so that is neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> The real question that exists with the WtA Lore is that since it is the only canon objective Lore in cWoD, should it be considered to be the default Lore of cWoD, with every other Lore being subjective interpretations of events from WtA Lore? If so, does that invalidate the nature of the other games or, because of the subjective nature of their Lore, is it a big shrug?<br /> <br /> For example, the conflicts between VtM Lore and WtA Lore primarily occur before the Great Flood and the destruction of the First City. If the Antediluvian Kindred, however, were exiles from the High Umbra (with the 'Gardens' of VtA Lore being different High Umbra Realms), then squaring the circle of VtM Lore and WtA Lore give Kindred spiritual legitimacy in the eyes of WtA Lore. Kindred would have a reason for existing and, while the Garou would still ash them for helping the Wyrm spread corruption, they would have to reluctantly admit that the Kindred were a High Umbra variation of the Possessed. Of course, the Kindred would not care either way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T07:33:47-08:00","id":1054304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054281#post1054281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that the Currs would be considered a Mockery Breed under current WtA Lore, so I doubt that they would have a sufficient connection to the spirit world to understand how wrong they are about Gaia. However, the Currs are not a canon Fera Breed, so that is neither here nor there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstand what they are. The Currs aren't a different breed of changers. They are garou who reject the culture of Garou Nation and are trying to destroy it. They have every spiritual and physical tool that the garou nation has.<br /> <br /> I brought them up in this threat as an alternative to the Nation or BSDs, playing up the negative image of the Nation and wish to correct/destroy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T07:58:58-08:00","id":1054317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054215#post1054215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Yeah. Someone start a new thread so I can rant about the mental gymnastics one has to perform to think allowing someone to get tortured is AOK at Humanity 9-10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the thread I started: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...er-expectation</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T01:20:16-08:00","id":1054679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1051955#post1051955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shattered Dreams' historical sections are really neat on being clear what was wrong, but portraying the situation as complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for saying so. We worked hard to make the history as rich as possible, and try to explain some of the deeply historic and cultural issues that are the roots of shapeshifters' modern problems.<br /> <br /> It's a pity that someone felt the need to slap 'non-canon' on it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T02:09:49-08:00","id":1054687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054679#post1054679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a pity that someone felt the need to slap 'non-canon' on it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>LoL wut? It's published by Onyx path!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T07:00:08-08:00","id":1054736,"title":"","content":"Yeah, how is Shattered Dreams non-canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:14:19-08:00","id":1054753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054736#post1054736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, how is Shattered Dreams non-canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because this is how it's presented on Drivethrurpg: &quot;Rather than one answer, it showcases many time periods and many ways in which the War could start, so that players and Storytellers can make prehistory their own.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it ends up being about as canon as the end books for the various lines (Apocalypse, Gehenna, etc.).<br /> <br /> ...which is more than a bit disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:30:12-08:00","id":1054762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054753#post1054753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it ends up being about as canon as the end books for the various lines (Apocalypse, Gehenna, etc.).<br /> <br /> ...which is more than a bit disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreement. I do not care for time travel as a device and I am glad they aren't something that is foisted on us. In any case, giving storytellers options without having any one choice be the expected outcome is fine with me. I liked the 'choose your own Apocalypse' take of the Time of Judgement books, and I liked elements of all of the WtA scenarios. However, I would never run any of them straight out of the box. But even if that toolkit approach leaves you lukewarm, can you imagine how many people would have been screaming when the single canon option inevitably rubbed a fair few folks the wrong way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-25-2017, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:57:18-08:00","id":1054816,"title":"","content":"I meant Shattered Dreams being non canon was disappointing. I completely understand the logic of the Apocalypse scenarios not having one canon choice. <br /> <br /> The time travel element is odd. But that section could have gotten the non canon tag (and should have) without doing so to the whole book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:09:26-08:00","id":1054822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture?p=1054816#post1054816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant Shattered Dreams being non canon was disappointing. I completely understand the logic of the Apocalypse scenarios not having one canon choice.<br /> <br /> The time travel element is odd. But that section could have gotten the non canon tag (and should have) without doing so to the whole book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, gotcha. I don't think that approach would have hurt things one bit. I guess the parts people wish were more canonical were the War of Rage and the Mokole stuff, then? That was all fine and dandy. I just wasn't so sure about Nightmaster using wormholes in the Abyss to alter the timeline; seemed like a pretty clumsy way to insert modern existing PCs into ancient history.<br /> <br /> Although, given the dearth of other depictions of events from the earliest history of the Fera... it seems like Shattered Dreams would be easy to default to, canon or no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:30:54-08:00","id":1054837,"title":"","content":"That part of the book with time traveling really turned me off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:34:07-08:00","id":1054842,"title":"","content":"<br /> I personally hate time travel and consider it to be a lazy narrative device.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:12:16-08:00","id":1054873,"title":"","content":"Yea, I just planned on ignoring the time travel bit and playing through past scenarios using the Ancestors concept that's already in the game. Should be good fun all around. I will just use the modern times player characters and switch a few dots of modern skills for antiquated ones and have the players play it out. It also plays into the theme of descendents following in the footsteps of their ancestors. Haven't thought the whole thing through just yet since I only started really reading through Shattered Dreams thoroughly this morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}